  "description": "Appointment application overview for tb-dev: backend/frontend/worker pods, Rollout and prePromotionAnalysis state, origin ALB, CloudFront, Celery worker health, migration Job outcome and namespace logs.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [
    {
      "asDropdown": false,
      "icon": "external link",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": false,
      "tags": [],
      "targetBlank": true,
      "title": "Issue #43 \u2014 Appointment stage dashboard",
      "tooltip": "",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "https://github.com/thunderbird/platform-grafana/issues/43"
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Appointment \u2014 tb-dev application overview\n\nBackend and frontend run as Argo Rollouts blue-green Rollouts in the `appointment` namespace (platform-infrastructure#781). Four things here need a second look before you trust what they show:\n\n- **Worker and Migration Job panels** \u2014 the Celery worker and the DB migration Job do not exist on tb-dev yet ([appointment-deploy#19](https://github.com/thunderbird/appointment-deploy/issues/19), [#20](https://github.com/thunderbird/appointment-deploy/issues/20)). Pod/Job name patterns below are best-guess, matching the existing `appointment-backend`/`appointment-frontend` convention, and may need adjusting once those manifests land.\n- **Rollout Phase and prePromotionAnalysis Result** \u2014 `rollout_info` and `analysis_run_info` are the right metrics, but the tb-dev argo-rollouts Helm release has `controller.metrics.enabled: false` and no ServiceMonitor, so neither is scraped yet. Both panels will start working once that's enabled in platform-infrastructure.\n- **Celery Worker Health** \u2014 the backend has no Prometheus client or task-metrics exporter at all, so this shows pod-level health only, never task throughput or failures.\n- **Origin ALB pickers** \u2014 the LoadBalancer and Target Group dropdowns below list every ALB and target group in the tb-dev eu-central-1 account, not just Appointment's, because no ARN is known to filter by. There is no default selection: confirm you've picked the appointment origin ALB before reading Target Health or 5xx Count.\n\n**Current Rollout revision** has no Prometheus equivalent by design (argo-rollouts never exposes it as a metric) \u2014 use the Rollouts link panel below, which is the live source for revision and blue-green step detail.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Prerequisites and how to read this dashboard",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 2,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Rollouts",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "Prometheus has no revision metric for Argo Rollouts \u2014 it is only ever a Kubernetes annotation. Use the live, read-only Rollouts dashboard for current revision, blue-green step state and full AnalysisRun detail:\n\n[appointment-backend](https://rollouts-tb-dev.pi.thunderbird.net/rollout/appointment/appointment-backend)  \u00b7  [appointment-frontend](https://rollouts-tb-dev.pi.thunderbird.net/rollout/appointment/appointment-frontend)",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Rollout revision and analysis detail",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "P4169E866C3094E38"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            },
            "inspect": false
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
